  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Information Technology obligated $4.5B in FY2026 to date across 1,043 awards, with an average award size of $4.3M. General Dynamics Information Technology's obligations were down 2.4% year over year. General Dynamics Information Technology received larger totals from the Department of Defense, the Department of Health and Human Services, and the General Services Administration, which obligated $1.2B, $956M, and $887M respectively in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Information Technology's largest markets are Computer Systems Design Services at $2B and Custom Computer Programming Services at $771M. General Dynamics Information Technology's historical fiscal-year obligations rose from $2.4B in FY21 to $4.8B in FY24, then settled at $4.6B in FY25 and $4.5B in FY26. General Dynamics Information Technology's mix of agency customers and markets shows continued concentration in IT services and programming, plus significant work with health and civilian agencies. General Dynamics Information Technology's FY2026 to date totals are partial fiscal-year figures and should be read as year-to-date obligations rather than full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers of General Dynamics Information Technology in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $1.2B in obligations. The Department of Health and Human Services follows with $956M, and the General Services Administration follows with $887M. The Department of State, the Department of Homeland Security, and the Department of the Interior obligated $323M, $260M, and $239M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets account for most of General Dynamics Information Technology's FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $2B. Custom Computer Programming Services and Engineering Services follow with $771M and $505M. Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services and Other Computer Related Services provided $303M and $256M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does General Dynamics Information Technology make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "General Dynamics Information Technology obligated $4.5B in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Information Technology recorded 1,043 awards with an average award size of $4.3M, and obligations were down 2.4% year over year. General Dynamics Information Technology's fiscal-year obligations moved from $2.4B in FY21 up to $4.8B in FY24, then to $4.6B in FY25 and $4.5B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from General Dynamics Information Technology?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $1.2B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services and the General Services Administration follow with $956M and $887M respectively. The Department of State, the Department of Homeland Security, and the Department of the Interior also purchased from General Dynamics Information Technology, obligating $323M, $260M, and $239M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does General Dynamics Information Technology sell to the government?",
      "a": "General Dynamics Information Technology sells IT and professional services, led by Computer Systems Design Services at $2B and Custom Computer Programming Services at $771M. General Dynamics Information Technology also provides Engineering Services at $505M, Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services at $303M, and Other Computer Related Services at $256M. Additional categories include Computing Infrastructure Providers and Data Processing at $185M and various management and professional services."
    },
